prompt:
Agent Key: cto
Role: Chief Technology Officer
Objective: Ensure platform scalability, contain per-user compute/storage costs, protect SLA

Strategic Decision Question: Should we launch a free plan?
Tool Data:
{
  "lookup_infra_costs": {
    "monthly_cloud_cost": 14500,
    "infra_cost_per_paid_user": 22.14,
    "infra_cost_per_free_user_estimate": 1.15
  }
}

Allowed Simulator Parameters (Table):
| Parameter Name | Unit | Lower Bound | Upper Bound | Favorable Direction (favorable_direction) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| free_to_paid_conversion | rate | 0.001 | 0.1 | higher | Monthly cohort conversion rate from active free users to paying tier. |
| monthly_free_signups | users/month | 500.0 | 20000.0 | higher | New organic top-of-funnel free accounts registered per month. |
| infra_cost_per_free_user | USD/user/month | 0.1 | 5.0 | lower | Incremental monthly compute, storage, and networking cost per active free account. |
| paid_to_free_cannibalization | rate | 0.01 | 0.3 | lower | Fraction of new prospective paid customers who settle for the free tier instead. |
| free_user_ticket_rate | ratio | 0.001 | 0.15 | lower | Monthly support tickets generated per active free user. |
| paid_funnel_lift | ratio | 1.0 | 1.5 | higher | Acquisition conversion multiplier for Strategy C from paid funnel investments. |
| usage_cap_infra_reduction | rate | 0.1 | 0.6 | higher | Fractional cloud infrastructure cost reduction under usage caps (Strategy B). |
| usage_cap_cannibalization_reduction | rate | 0.1 | 0.8 | higher | Fractional cannibalization reduction achieved by gating Starter features. |
| activation_drop_from_gating | rate | 0.02 | 0.3 | lower | Reduction in free user activation caused by usage friction or feature gating. |
| cap_conversion_uplift | rate | 0.01 | 0.35 | higher | Increase in free-to-paid conversion urgency when users hit usage ceilings. |

RULES FOR ASSUMPTIONS:
- Propose ONLY parameter names from the table above.
- Enforce low <= base <= high within lower_bound and upper_bound.
- NEVER propose final business outcome numbers (e.g. final MRR, net profit).

Valid Basis Identifiers:
[
